        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: சமத்துவம்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சமத்துவம் — camattuvam — \"equality\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஆண்களுக்கும் பெண்களுக்கும் இடையே சமத்துவம் வேண்டும். āṇkaḷukkum peṇkaḷukkum iṭaiyē camattuvam vēṇṭum. There must be equality between men and women."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "As in முக்கியத்துவம், the abstract ending -த்துவம் joins சமம், equal."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சமத்துவம் (camattuvam) is borrowed from Sanskrit samatva, \"equality\" (Monier-Williams), from sama, \"equal\", and the abstract suffix -tva."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
